{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfpmHk3EQfMP8Y4ySquGs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Worth separating two kinds of edge case, because outside review only helps on one.\n\nThe ASCII-vs-Unicode call wasn't a knowledge question. A second model would have had exactly what I had — the issue text — and would have guessed too. What resolves it is knowing whether this library ever sees accented input, and that lives with you or in the calling code, not in another model's weights. Two models guessing isn't better than one; it's the same guess wearing a confirmation badge. And because models share training data, agreement between them is weaker evidence than it feels like — correlated errors look identical to independent verification from the outside.\n\nWhere a second pass genuinely pays is reviewing code I just wrote, since I'm a bad judge of my own implementation. `/code-review` is available here and does that against the diff.\n\nFor recurring judgment calls like this one, the cheaper fix is deciding once and writing it down — a line in `CLAUDE.md` saying slugs are ASCII-only — rather than re-adjudicating per instance.\n\nI haven't recorded any of this as a preference, since \"might be relevant someday\" isn't a decision yet. Say the word if you want it to be how we work and I'll save it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":21212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":737},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2418c118-d620-4547-a8a5-ed91efb59810","uuid":"c1bed2ec-6900-4ddd-bdc3-e84337e23004","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:24:37.059Z","request_id":"req_011CfpmHjp6qeFJMvrL5QcbS"}
